00:20.510 --> 00:21.870
Could she be...

01:53.250 --> 01:58.260
Downsizing Game

01:54.140 --> 01:56.180
There'll be eight winners?

01:56.620 --> 01:58.070
Hang on a minute!

01:58.070 --> 01:59.630
That's not what we signed up for!

02:00.530 --> 02:01.880
I beg your pardon?

02:01.880 --> 02:05.470
Everyone here lost the second-round game!

02:05.470 --> 02:07.260
We're at least 100 million in the hole!

02:07.550 --> 02:11.770
We were told we could wipe
 our debts clean if we came here!

02:12.140 --> 02:16.030
That description is not incorrect.

02:16.030 --> 02:17.750
The hell it's not!

02:17.750 --> 02:19.530
Is there a prize or isn't there?!

02:19.820 --> 02:23.060
The loser will be forced to 
surrender 100 million yen.

02:23.060 --> 02:26.110
That 100 million will be split 
among the eight winners.

02:26.640 --> 02:28.490
That is the prize.

02:29.240 --> 02:32.120
So we'd only get 12.5 million each?

02:32.120 --> 02:34.210
That's barely a drop in the bucket!

02:34.210 --> 02:36.040
You are mistaken.

02:36.310 --> 02:40.800
The prize is not the only way 
to make money in this game.

02:44.030 --> 02:48.130
As you can see, the venue is barren.

02:48.450 --> 02:51.860
Neither food nor drinking
 water are available.

02:52.400 --> 02:57.350
To survive this game, you will find 
yourselves needing various things.

02:58.070 --> 03:02.530
You may use your M Tickets 
to purchase these things.

03:02.530 --> 03:06.380
For instance, let us say you are 
desperate for a drink of water.

03:06.380 --> 03:11.000
Another player offers 
it to you for 500 yen.

03:11.000 --> 03:13.200
You agree to this deal.

03:13.670 --> 03:23.200
Transaction with: Takahiro Kikuzawa

03:13.670 --> 03:23.200
Terms

03:13.670 --> 03:23.200
Terms

03:13.670 --> 03:23.200
Amount

03:13.670 --> 03:23.200
Amount

03:13.670 --> 03:23.200
Hiroto Kitamura

03:13.670 --> 03:23.200
Takahiro Kikuzawa

03:13.670 --> 03:23.200
Sell one bottle of water

03:13.670 --> 03:23.200
Buy one bottle of water

03:13.670 --> 03:23.200
Transaction with: Hiroto Kitamura

03:13.890 --> 03:17.150
At this time, both buyer 
and seller will write

03:17.150 --> 03:20.990
the terms of their exchange and
the arranged price on their M Tickets.

03:20.990 --> 03:25.010
A tournament official will certify them,
thus completing the trade.

03:25.430 --> 03:29.030
Anyone who fails to fulfill 
their part of such a deal

03:29.030 --> 03:31.620
will be issued a penalty 
of 100 million yen.

03:32.400 --> 03:37.290
Those who find the prize insufficient 
need only sell what they can to earn more.

03:37.290 --> 03:41.150
You can buy or sell absolutely 
anything with M Tickets.

03:41.150 --> 03:44.400
They did mention that 
on the invitation...

03:41.150 --> 03:47.160
The Losers' Revival Match will begin at the date, time, and place listed here.

03:41.150 --> 03:47.160
Please scan this QR code

03:41.150 --> 03:47.160
Please be on time. You may bring anything to the venue, excluding illegal 
items (guns, bladed weapons, narcotics, stimulants, etc.).
 To ensure your victory, we recommend that you come fully prepared.

03:44.400 --> 03:46.700
That we could bring anything in with us.

03:49.200 --> 03:53.370
I didn't bring anything 
anyone would want to buy.

03:53.660 --> 03:57.380
There's not a damn thing we could bring 
that'd fetch hundreds of millions!

03:57.380 --> 03:58.800
Damn it all!

03:59.060 --> 04:01.890
All will become clear 
once the game begins.

04:01.890 --> 04:06.000
The most unexpected things may 
fetch a high price indeed.

04:08.980 --> 04:13.630
Now, allow me to move on 
to an explanation of the game.

04:14.740 --> 04:16.860
This is an L Ticket.

04:16.860 --> 04:19.940
It is a ballot slip with 
five spaces for names.

04:20.130 --> 04:22.060
In these spaces,

04:22.060 --> 04:26.320
you will write the names of players you 
wish to see move on to the third game.

04:26.620 --> 04:28.720
Nao Kanzaki

04:26.620 --> 04:28.720
Takayoshi Miura

04:26.620 --> 04:28.720
Hiroto Kitamura

04:26.620 --> 04:28.720
Teruyuki Eda

04:26.620 --> 04:28.720
Yuji Fukunaga

04:26.800 --> 04:31.010
You may write the same name 
five times if you wish.

04:28.490 --> 04:31.450
Nao Kanzaki

04:28.490 --> 04:31.450
Nao Kanzaki

04:28.490 --> 04:31.450
Nao Kanzaki

04:28.490 --> 04:31.450
Nao Kanzaki

04:28.490 --> 04:31.450
Nao Kanzaki

04:31.450 --> 04:34.640
However, you may not write your own name,

04:34.640 --> 04:37.030
nor may you write ineligible names.

04:37.700 --> 04:42.330
You will vote once per hour, 
for a total of ten times.

04:42.720 --> 04:45.100
Then, once the voting is complete,

04:45.350 --> 04:49.150
the player with the fewest 
votes will be downsized.

04:49.820 --> 04:51.840
They will be declared the loser.

04:53.490 --> 04:57.100
Now, let the game begin!

04:57.400 --> 05:01.210
The first vote will take place
 three hours from now.

05:04.760 --> 05:08.860
Even if I won, I'd still 
only earn 12.5 million...

05:09.730 --> 05:13.030
That's not nearly enough 
to save Akiyama-san.

05:13.840 --> 05:16.400
And these M Tickets...

05:16.890 --> 05:19.860
Will I really find a way to utilize 
them before the game ends?

05:21.490 --> 05:23.860
Plus, there's one other 
thing I don't understand.

05:24.160 --> 05:26.750
Everyone here seems so strangely calm.

05:27.340 --> 05:31.730
It's as if they all feel assured 
of their victory...

05:32.550 --> 05:34.070
Heya, Nao-chan.

05:34.850 --> 05:36.640
Need a drink?

05:36.640 --> 05:37.900
Miura-san?

05:37.900 --> 05:39.490
I've got a whole selection!

05:39.490 --> 05:42.370
There's mineral water, 
there's ginger ale...

05:42.370 --> 05:44.920
All the vending machines here are busted.

05:44.920 --> 05:46.770
N-Not at the moment.

05:47.350 --> 05:48.560
Sheesh.

05:48.560 --> 05:51.530
I'm not gonna earn squat
with these M Tickets.

05:52.220 --> 05:55.850
Um, can I ask why you seem so calm?

05:56.580 --> 05:58.940
You and everyone else here...

06:00.260 --> 06:01.950
Why d'you think?

06:01.950 --> 06:04.520
We all know who's gonna lose.

06:06.150 --> 06:08.830
Fukunaga's getting downsized hard.

06:08.830 --> 06:12.630
Everyone agrees on that.

06:14.070 --> 06:16.080
The eight of us here besides you...

06:16.080 --> 06:18.690
We were all in the same group
 for the second game.

06:18.690 --> 06:20.560
Oh, that's right!

06:21.180 --> 06:27.130
And you probably know that every last 
one of us ended up 100 mil in the red.

06:27.770 --> 06:32.860
I'd like to do a whole lot more 
than just see that little weasel lose.

06:33.630 --> 06:36.800
I'd dish out a whole bloody 
beating if I could.

06:38.080 --> 06:42.640
I see it now. They're all 
clearly avoiding Fukunaga-san.

06:43.700 --> 06:47.220
I get it. If I were in their shoes...

06:48.320 --> 06:50.550
Okay, everyone. Listen up.

06:50.860 --> 06:53.730
We have three whole hours before the vote.

06:53.730 --> 06:55.560
To kill time before then...

06:55.970 --> 06:58.920
How about we hold a little pitch meeting?

06:59.550 --> 07:03.230
Pitch meeting? The hell?

07:03.230 --> 07:05.560
So that we can all make our case.

07:05.560 --> 07:09.160
About how much we want to win.

07:09.730 --> 07:12.990
Take your little schemes and shove 'em!

07:12.990 --> 07:15.700
You're not changing what 
we've all agreed on!

07:15.700 --> 07:18.070
That you're going down!

07:19.780 --> 07:21.970
Perfectly fine by me.

07:23.070 --> 07:24.960
Don't go getting the wrong idea.

07:24.960 --> 07:28.410
I'm genuinely just trying to kill time.

07:28.410 --> 07:31.780
I'm fully aware that I'm 
walking out of here a loser.

07:32.920 --> 07:35.480
But what about the rest of you?

07:35.480 --> 07:39.470
Come the third game, you'll be
 back to fighting each other.

07:39.470 --> 07:44.360
When that happens, you'll need
 to figure out who to cut loose.

07:44.680 --> 07:47.640
You should use this time to consider it...

07:48.310 --> 07:52.680
"Who's on the chopping block after her?"

07:54.480 --> 07:56.400
Yeah, I guess.

07:56.400 --> 08:00.210
Not like we have much 
else to do for three hours.

08:03.890 --> 08:07.030
And so the pitch meeting began.

08:07.810 --> 08:10.560
Everyone had their reasons 
for wanting to win.

08:11.350 --> 08:14.320
"I'll never reach my dream
 if I go bankrupt."

08:14.320 --> 08:15.860
"It'll upset my parents."

08:16.800 --> 08:20.810
Everyone made a desperate pitch 
in the hopes of their own survival.

08:21.930 --> 08:24.530
And when my turn came...

08:24.530 --> 08:25.470
May I ask a question?

08:26.350 --> 08:28.930
What exactly are you doing here?

08:28.930 --> 08:32.190
What do you mean? 
A tournament official came by...

08:32.190 --> 08:34.740
You know that's not what I mean.

08:35.080 --> 08:37.730
How deep in debt are you again?

08:37.980 --> 08:40.620
I'm not in any debt.

08:42.380 --> 08:45.120
What? No debt at all?!

08:43.020 --> 08:44.050
She's not...

08:44.050 --> 08:45.120
...in debt?

08:45.420 --> 08:50.760
Wait, are you telling me you 
won big in the second game?

08:51.320 --> 08:52.260
Yes.

08:53.260 --> 08:56.200
But you knew that, didn't you?

08:56.200 --> 08:58.390
Hey, everyone, did you hear that?!

08:58.390 --> 09:01.720
She's not like us at all!

09:01.720 --> 09:06.490
Not only is she not in debt, 
but she made bank in the second game!

09:07.870 --> 09:09.350
In that instant...

09:12.360 --> 09:15.090
I could tell that the way 
they looked at me changed.

09:18.550 --> 09:21.040
That's all I needed to know.

09:21.310 --> 09:24.220
I can't wait to hear why you're playing,

09:24.220 --> 09:26.830
even though you're already 
swimming in cash.

09:26.830 --> 09:29.040
Go on, make your pitch!

09:33.800 --> 09:36.290
I was trapped.

09:37.040 --> 09:39.690
Fukunaga-san had planned this all out.

09:40.600 --> 09:44.350
The feeling in the hall, 
united against her up to that point...

09:45.310 --> 09:50.460
suddenly turned against me instead.

09:54.140 --> 09:57.830
You've become the odd woman out, Nao.

09:58.350 --> 09:59.940
Fukunaga-san!

09:59.940 --> 10:02.510
You tricked me, didn't you?!

10:04.060 --> 10:05.460
I most certainly did.

10:05.940 --> 10:08.780
But not just you.

10:09.820 --> 10:12.340
I tricked everyone else, too!

10:12.340 --> 10:14.480
Wh-What do you mean?

10:16.450 --> 10:19.100
All of that was just a feint.

10:19.340 --> 10:23.220
I've cleared a guaranteed 
path to victory for us.

10:24.280 --> 10:26.840
Did you say... "us"?

10:28.670 --> 10:31.640
There's a surefire way to win this game.

10:32.490 --> 10:36.570
If the vote were about who to downsize,

10:36.570 --> 10:39.400
either you or I would inevitably lose.

10:39.830 --> 10:42.230
But that's not how the game works.

10:42.570 --> 10:48.020
We vote for who, besides ourselves, 
we'd like to see go on to the third game,

10:48.020 --> 10:51.140
and the person with the 
fewest votes gets downsized.

10:51.610 --> 10:52.750
Right...

10:52.750 --> 10:54.570
Which makes it simple.

10:54.570 --> 10:58.500
You and I need only vote for each other.

10:58.500 --> 11:03.150
I'll write your name in all 
five slots on my L Tickets.

10:58.510 --> 11:03.700
Nao Kanzaki

10:58.510 --> 11:03.700
Nao Kanzaki

10:58.510 --> 11:03.700
Nao Kanzaki

10:58.510 --> 11:03.700
Nao Kanzaki

10:58.510 --> 11:03.700
Nao Kanzaki

11:03.030 --> 11:06.930
Yuji Fukunaga

11:03.030 --> 11:06.930
Yuji Fukunaga

11:03.030 --> 11:06.930
Yuji Fukunaga

11:03.030 --> 11:06.930
Yuji Fukunaga

11:03.030 --> 11:06.930
Yuji Fukunaga

11:03.150 --> 11:06.350
In exchange, you do the same for me.

11:06.940 --> 11:09.430
How many votes will that earn us?

11:09.980 --> 11:13.140
Ten rounds of five votes each...

11:13.140 --> 11:14.280
Fifty votes.

11:14.280 --> 11:15.190
Exactly.

11:15.450 --> 11:21.060
And in this game, once you have 
fifty votes, it's impossible to lose.

11:22.440 --> 11:25.220
There are nine players here, 
each with fifty votes to spend.

11:22.450 --> 11:50.230
Votes Cast

11:22.450 --> 11:50.230
Votes Held

11:25.220 --> 11:27.520
That's 450 votes available.

11:27.520 --> 11:30.830
You and I guarantee 
each other fifty votes.

11:30.830 --> 11:33.130
For us to be at the bottom,

11:33.130 --> 11:37.580
all the remaining players would 
have to secure 51 votes each.

11:38.070 --> 11:39.260
Is that doable?

11:39.260 --> 11:40.720
Well...

11:40.720 --> 11:44.470
For the remaining seven players 
to get 51 votes each,

11:44.470 --> 11:48.010
there would have to be 
a total pool of 457 votes.

11:48.010 --> 11:50.230
So it's not possible!

11:50.230 --> 11:51.400
That's right.

11:51.400 --> 11:53.470
Which means we can't conceivably lose.

11:53.470 --> 11:55.880
It's in the bag!

11:56.850 --> 12:01.010
But what if everyone ties at fifty votes?

12:01.010 --> 12:04.990
I held the pitch meeting to 
eliminate any chance of that.

12:05.460 --> 12:10.440
I intentionally singled you out
 to set you up as a heel.

12:10.440 --> 12:12.660
But that works in our favor!

12:13.620 --> 12:19.350
There are now two heels 
in the venue—both of us.

12:19.750 --> 12:25.250
They'll think, "One of them is sure to get
downsized. I don't have to do anything."

12:25.250 --> 12:32.260
A single heel wouldn't create that 
sense of safety, but two heels would.

12:32.820 --> 12:37.680
"If the two of them trade votes, 
they're guaranteed to win."

12:37.680 --> 12:40.650
They'd figure it out if they 
really thought about it.

12:40.650 --> 12:44.620
But their sense of safety will prevent 
them from even thinking that far ahead.

12:44.620 --> 12:46.910
And what will happen as a result?

12:47.260 --> 12:51.570
In the first vote, someone will 
end up with fewer than five votes.

12:52.420 --> 12:56.170
That's when the true horror 
of the game kicks in.

12:56.580 --> 13:01.670
Whoever falls behind in the first 
vote will never climb back up.

13:02.230 --> 13:05.020
After all, even if they trade votes,

13:05.020 --> 13:09.430
they can never reach 
the fifty-vote safe zone.

13:09.860 --> 13:15.180
So whoever's at the bottom in the first 
vote has a 100% chance of losing.

13:15.780 --> 13:17.070
By that same token...

13:17.480 --> 13:21.320
you and I have a 100% chance of victory!

13:21.720 --> 13:23.200
Amazing.

13:23.200 --> 13:25.780
So, do you agree to my plan?

13:26.270 --> 13:27.940
Yes, of course I do!

13:27.940 --> 13:29.390
Excellent.

13:29.390 --> 13:31.940
Well, the vote is in two hours.

13:32.320 --> 13:35.030
You know what to do when the time comes.

13:35.980 --> 13:37.580
Oh, and while I'm at it...

13:37.580 --> 13:41.530
Don't tell anyone about this, all right?

13:42.130 --> 13:43.090
Right!

13:44.190 --> 13:46.410
See you in two hours.

13:46.410 --> 13:48.550
U-Um, Fukunaga-san...

13:50.120 --> 13:51.930
Thank you very much...

13:51.930 --> 13:53.510
for saving me.

13:55.570 --> 13:57.460
Likewise, of course.

13:57.460 --> 14:00.570
We're both in the lurch. 
We have to help each other out.

14:03.760 --> 14:05.650
The time has arrived.

14:05.650 --> 14:09.360
We will now hold the first vote.

14:25.140 --> 14:28.830
At the very least, now I won't lose.

14:31.770 --> 14:34.280
We will now tally the votes.

14:35.470 --> 14:38.710
Eda. Fukunaga.

14:39.680 --> 14:40.840
Tsunoda.

14:39.690 --> 14:41.940
Teruyuki Eda


 Yuji Fukunaga


 Kosuke Tsunoda


 Hiroto Kitamura


 Tetsuzo Sato

14:41.940 --> 14:43.120
Kitamura.

14:43.990 --> 14:45.110
Miura.

14:45.930 --> 14:47.180
Sato.

14:47.940 --> 14:49.220
Fujita.

14:50.180 --> 14:51.440
Fukunaga.

14:52.240 --> 14:53.330
Eda.

15:00.030 --> 15:01.850
This concludes the voting.

15:02.250 --> 15:05.270
Yuji Fukunaga



 Hiroto Kitamura


Kosuke Tsunoda



 Tetsuzo Sato


 Takayoshi Miura



 Shingo Fujita


Teruyuki Eda



 Takahiro Kikuzawa


 Nao Kanzaki

15:02.260 --> 15:04.630
The result is as you see here.

15:04.770 --> 15:06.480
Nao Kanzaki

15:08.830 --> 15:11.290
Wh-What's going on?

15:11.290 --> 15:13.740
Why do I have zero votes?

15:14.380 --> 15:17.640
The next vote will take place in an hour.

15:15.010 --> 15:18.110
No... No...

15:17.640 --> 15:20.050
Let us meet again then.

15:22.290 --> 15:24.890
Fukunaga-san! 
Explain yourself this instant!

15:24.890 --> 15:28.650
You promised you'd give me five votes!

15:31.090 --> 15:33.290
I did make that promise, yes.

15:33.750 --> 15:36.540
But I was never going to keep it.

15:37.070 --> 15:38.930
This is the Liar Game.

15:38.930 --> 15:41.290
And you've been lied to...

15:41.290 --> 15:43.660
by me!

15:53.660 --> 15:56.990
She got me. She got me again...

15:58.320 --> 16:01.310
No, now's not the time to break down.

16:01.680 --> 16:04.010
We'll be voting nine more times.

16:04.430 --> 16:08.820
I have to ask the others to vote for me!

16:09.390 --> 16:10.600
Excuse me.

16:12.260 --> 16:14.650
Excuse me. I'd like to talk—

16:16.820 --> 16:19.840
Why? Why is everyone walking away?

16:21.940 --> 16:23.220
The time has arrived.

16:23.220 --> 16:26.150
We will now hold the second vote.

16:26.150 --> 16:27.410
No!

16:27.410 --> 16:29.920
I haven't done anything yet!

16:30.420 --> 16:35.430
Yuji Fukunaga



 Hiroto Kitamura


Kosuke Tsunoda


 Tetsuzo Sato



 Takayoshi Miura


 Shingo Fujita


Teruyuki Eda



 Takahiro Kikuzawa


 Nao Kanzaki

16:31.170 --> 16:34.650
The second vote was as cruel as the first.

16:36.350 --> 16:39.190
What Fukunaga-san had 
predicted became reality.

16:39.680 --> 16:48.440
Nao Kanzaki

16:39.690 --> 16:43.020
I'd fallen to the bottom 
in the first vote,

16:43.020 --> 16:46.430
and I didn't get a single vote 
the second time through.

16:48.020 --> 16:50.680
Someone, please help me!

16:50.680 --> 16:52.700
At least talk to me!

16:55.570 --> 17:00.080
Yuji Fukunaga




Tetsuzo Sato



 Takayoshi Miura



 Shingo Fujita


 Hiroto Kitamura


 Kosuke Tsunoda

 Teruyuki Eda

 Takahiro Kikuzawa


 Nao Kanzaki

16:56.320 --> 16:59.330
Third Vote

17:03.680 --> 17:04.940
Have some.

17:05.690 --> 17:07.500
I'm not gonna charge you.

17:08.660 --> 17:09.980
Miura-san...

17:09.980 --> 17:11.200
Thank you.

17:11.200 --> 17:12.750
No need to thank me.

17:13.140 --> 17:16.910
I'd throw some votes your way if I could.

17:16.910 --> 17:19.030
I just can't.

17:19.030 --> 17:20.550
What do you mean?

17:21.680 --> 17:23.770
Man, you've really got no clue...

17:24.830 --> 17:29.060
You made a deal with Fukunaga 
to vote for each other, right?

17:29.370 --> 17:32.270
Yes. She said it was guaranteed.

17:32.880 --> 17:37.240
The rest of us had the same idea.

17:37.530 --> 17:42.770
We were all gonna trade 
votes in small groups

17:42.770 --> 17:46.560
to ensure either you or Fukunaga lost.

17:48.220 --> 17:50.030
What are we whispering about?

17:50.260 --> 17:52.010
Let me guess.

17:52.290 --> 17:56.010
You're discussing your 
approach to this game.

17:56.010 --> 17:59.810
You'll break into groups of 
two or three, trade votes,

17:59.810 --> 18:02.420
and guarantee fifty votes for each of you.

18:02.420 --> 18:04.990
Thus, you'll take down either Nao or me.

18:07.320 --> 18:10.480
Did you really think you 
could ride it out that way?

18:10.480 --> 18:12.000
Of course we can!

18:12.000 --> 18:15.740
As long as we get fifty votes, 
we can't possibly lose!

18:15.970 --> 18:18.620
You certainly can't lose that way, true.

18:18.920 --> 18:22.620
But what if Nao and I 
made a pact of our own?

18:23.560 --> 18:25.230
Hang on, did you...

18:25.700 --> 18:28.700
That's right. We're working together.

18:28.990 --> 18:31.720
Now you can't possibly win.

18:31.720 --> 18:37.390
On the contrary, one of you 
is guaranteed to lose.

18:37.390 --> 18:39.560
Huh? Whaddya mean by that?!

18:39.560 --> 18:43.000
Nao Kanzaki has money, remember?

18:43.590 --> 18:47.680
Once the deadlock becomes clear,
 she'll make her move.

18:47.680 --> 18:50.530
She'll shave one of you off from the rest.

18:50.530 --> 18:52.020
Shave one of us off?

18:52.330 --> 18:54.790
She'll propose a betrayal.

18:54.790 --> 19:00.330
"I'll give you 40 million yen if 
you cast a single vote for me."

19:00.750 --> 19:03.660
I'd... I'd never betray anyone.

19:03.660 --> 19:09.470
Maybe you wouldn't, but can you 
be so sure about your partner?

19:11.390 --> 19:17.300
In a game with a meager prize of 12.5 mil,
 another 40 would go a long way.

19:17.880 --> 19:24.410
How many people here could 
say no to such a juicy offer?

19:25.420 --> 19:29.260
Now, it might sound like 
I'm here to scare you...

19:29.950 --> 19:33.930
but I actually want to help you.

19:35.600 --> 19:37.430
Pay me 5 million each,

19:37.780 --> 19:40.780
for a total of 35 million,

19:40.780 --> 19:43.330
and I'll save you all.

19:43.850 --> 19:46.510
Save us? How?

19:47.370 --> 19:50.590
I'll stab Nao Kanzaki in the back.

19:51.830 --> 19:55.310
I'll give my fifty votes to you.

19:55.310 --> 19:59.820
Then Nao Kanzaki is guaranteed 
to receive zero votes and lose.

19:59.820 --> 20:02.730
Meanwhile, your survival is guaranteed.

20:02.970 --> 20:05.420
But where do we get the five million?

20:05.420 --> 20:07.240
Oh, you know where!

20:08.050 --> 20:11.920
You can buy my betrayal with these.

20:12.810 --> 20:16.500
What did you think these 
M Tickets were for?

20:16.500 --> 20:18.520
Think back.

20:18.770 --> 20:23.560
To survive this game, you will find 
yourselves needing various things.

20:24.140 --> 20:28.530
You may use your M Tickets 
to purchase these things.

20:29.110 --> 20:34.230
The thing you need most in 
this game isn't water or food.

20:34.920 --> 20:36.710
It's strategy.

20:37.030 --> 20:40.360
Strategy, tactics, foolproof plans...

20:40.360 --> 20:43.960
Abstract concepts, to be sure, 
but they go for a premium here.

20:44.440 --> 20:47.330
That's what this game is all about.

20:48.170 --> 20:51.820
So, what do you think of my plan?

20:51.820 --> 20:54.370
Will you buy in? Or no deal?

20:56.670 --> 21:01.130
We all bought in on Fukunaga's plan.

21:03.470 --> 21:07.900
She's using the M Tickets like contracts.

21:07.900 --> 21:11.580
I'm swapping my votes with Fukunaga.

21:07.910 --> 21:12.270
Transaction with: Fukunaga

